e a knight } 17. Ne1 { [%clk 0:02:53] } Be8 { [%clk 0:04:24] } 18. h3 { [%clk 0:02:50] with Kh2 ideas. } Nd7 { [%clk 0:04:18] } 19. Nxd7 { [%clk 0:02:45] } Bxd7 { [%clk 0:04:17] knight for knight trade. Now after LSB for knight we achieve our objective of knight vs bad bishop. } 20. Nf3 { [%clk 0:02:45] } Qg6 { [%clk 0:04:14] } 21. Ne5 { [%clk 0:02:43] } Qe8 { [%clk 0:04:11] } 22. Bxe4 { [%clk 0:02:34] leaving us with a favorable good knight vs bad bishop imbalance. Also, preventing him maneuvering his knight to remove ours. } (22. Kh2 Nd6 23. Rg1 Nf7 24. g4 Nxe5 25. dxe5 { we wanted to avoid losing the good knight vs bad bishop imbalance. }) 22... fxe4 { [%clk 0:04:10] And voila. We have a monster knight vs a bad bishop. } 23. g4 { [%clk 0:02:18] Aman doesn't explain this pawn break but it is the 2nd best engine move. } Bc8 { [%clk 0:04:09] } 24. Rf2 { [%clk 0:02:12] } b5 { [%clk 0:04:07] } 25. cxb5 { [%clk 0:02:08] } cxb5 { [%clk 0:04:07] And the purpose behind the earlier Rac1 move becomes clear as the c file opens. } 26. Rc7 { [%clk 0:01:47] Immediately infiltrating and preventing Bc7. } (26. Rfc2 Bb7 27. Rc7 Rc8 { Aman was concerned about this. }) 26... b4 { [%clk 0:04:01] } 27. Rfc2 { [%clk 0:01:35] } Ba6 { [%clk 0:03:59] Bishop to the queen side which the engine thinks is the best move. Aman thinks it's bad though as he's about to apply a lot of pressure to the king side. } 28. Qg3 { [%clk 0:01:16] with Qh4... Qg5 ideas. } Bd3?? { [%clk 0:03:45] a 1 move threat achieving nothing. } 29. R2c6 { [%clk 0:01:12] } a5 { [%clk 0:03:40] } 30. Qh4 { [%clk 0:01:08] } Qd8 { [%clk 0:03:26] preventing Qg5 } 31. Qh5 { [%clk 0:00:58] } a4 { [%clk 0:03:22] } 32. Rd7 { [%clk 0:00:56] With Rcc7 ideas } Qe8?? { [%clk 0:03:16] blunders mate in seven } 33. Rxg7+ { [%clk 0:00:48] } Kxg7 { [%clk 0:03:09] } 34. Rc7+ { [%clk 0:00:47] } Rf7 { [%clk 0:03:02] } 35. Rxf7+ { [%clk 0:00:44] } Qxf7 { [%clk 0:03:01] } 36. Qxf7+ { [%clk 0:00:44] Opponent resigns facing mate in four on the board. } 1-0

